---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
	title="Ceramics departments at schools and colleges"
	description="Manage wheel bookings between classes, kiln firing queues and multi-week ceramics courses for your school or college department."
>
	<section class="band-dark page-hero">
		<div class="wrap split">
			<div>
				<p class="eyebrow">Schools &amp; colleges</p>
				<h1>Make room for clay between classes.</h1>
				<p class="lede">
					One or two kilns, a semester timetable and students looking for wheel time. Bring
					bookings, firings and ceramics courses together with Kilnbook.
				</p>
			</div>
			<img
				src="/images/wheel-grid.svg"
				alt="A day view of four wheels booked in one-hour blocks from 9am to 6pm"
				width="480"
				height="300"
			/>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="wrap section narrow">
		<h2>Wheel time between lectures</h2>
		<p>
			Students can reserve a wheel in one-hour blocks for practice between classes. Set booking
			hours and advance booking limits per membership tier, and give shared equipment its own
			calendar. <a href="/features/wheel-time">See wheel and table booking</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Keep the kiln queue moving</h2>
		<p>
			With one or two kilns serving a whole department, it helps to know what is waiting for
			bisque and what is ready for glaze. Each kiln gets its own queues and a firing log with
			the date, cone, schedule and who loaded it. Students get a pickup text when their load is
			unloaded. <a href="/features/firings">Explore kiln firings</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Courses for the semester timetable</h2>
		<p>
			Set up a fixed series of ceramics sessions for a multi-week course, or offer drop-ins for
			extra practice. Instructors can see their roster, mark attendance and leave notes for the
			next instructor. Waitlists offer cancelled seats to the next student in line.
			<a href="/features/classes">See classes and class packs</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>A plan for your department</h2>
		<p>
			The Studio plan covers up to 3 kilns, with unlimited members, wheel and table reservations,
			class packs and waitlists. That gives a department running one or two kilns room for a
			third. <a href="/pricing">Compare plans</a>.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="section section-alt">
		<div class="wrap narrow">
			<h2>Questions departments ask</h2>
			<details>
				<summary>Which plan fits a department with two kilns?</summary>
				<p>
					Studio covers up to 3 kilns and includes wheel and table reservations. Starter covers
					1 kiln, while Collective has unlimited kilns. See the <a href="/pricing">plan details</a>.
				</p>
			</details>
			<details>
				<summary>Can students book wheels between classes?</summary>
				<p>
					Yes. Students reserve wheels in one-hour blocks. You decide how many hours each
					membership tier gets and how far ahead they can book.
				</p>
			</details>
			<details>
				<summary>Is there a discount for school ceramics programs?</summary>
				<p>
					School ceramics programs get 30% off any plan. Mention your program when you book a demo.
				</p>
			</details>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="cta-band">
		<div class="wrap">
			<h2>Bring your semester timetable.</h2>
			<p>Talk through wheel bookings, courses and the kiln queue for your department.</p>
			<a href="/contact" class="btn btn-dark">Book a demo</a>
		</div>
	</section>
</Base>
